# Cursor rules — Servicio Técnico de Celulares
Read AI_CONTEXT.md before any change. It overrides any conflicting prompt.
Then read ai-context/constitution/00-general.md and backend.md.

Non-negotiables:
- Docs in Spanish, code in English (GEN-01). TypeScript strict, no `any` (GEN-05).
- controller → service → repository → Prisma. PrismaService only in repositories (BE-05, BE-08).
- Every input goes through a class-validator DTO; every handler has @Roles (BE-10, BE-29).
- WorkOrder.status is written ONLY by WorkOrderTransitionService (RN-04).
- Stock mutations: guarded updateMany inside $transaction + kardex row (BE-16, RN-09).
- Unlock codes: AES-256-GCM via UnlockCodeCipher, never logged or serialized (RN-03).
- Audit table and kardex are append-only (RN-12, BE-17).
- Money is Prisma.Decimal, never Float (RN-15).
- Every service/hook/domain function ships with Jest unit tests citing the RN.
- Never run `prisma migrate`, `db push` or destructive SQL without explicit human confirmation.
